Error [E-OSTARGET-DISPATCH-ARM]: `.Bsd` is not an OS arm — a `build.os` dispatch matches `.Linux`, `.MacOS`, or `.Windows`
  --> tests/ui/os_target_dispatch_bad_arm.jet:12:9
    |
 12 |         .Bsd -> {
    |         ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: each arm gates code for exactly one native OS, so its head is a bare, payload-free OS variant — the same set `#Target(OS.*)` uses — and each OS appears at most once
 Fix: write `.Linux -> …`, `.MacOS -> …`, or `.Windows -> …` (add an `else -> …` for a shared fallback)
